{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Do not see.</b> For us: do not prophesy." "And they are called <b>seers</b> because prophecy is through visions of Elohim." "<b> Straight things.</b> Like דבריך ישרי׳ ונכוחים (your words are straight and direct) (2 Samuel 15:3), and it is an adjective." "<b>Smooth things.</b> Likewise 'see delusions':"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {2 "Ibn Ezra quotes דבריך; the printed text reads דברים, corrected per the footnote צ״ל."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:57.784622269Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}